<http://unnethack.wordpress.com/2010/03/03/lost/>

Have you ever searched for a fountain you knew you encountered some levels
ago?

Have you ever forgotten the location of your stashes?

Have you ever taken notes because you feared to not remember how the dungeon
looked like if you take a break from playing?

In short, have you ever been /lost/ in the Dungeons of Doom?

As often is the case with NetHack, there's a patch for that!

Hojita Discordia made the Dungeon Map Overview patch
<http://bilious.homelinux.org/?267>. There's also a Slash'Em version of this
patch <http://bamgames.free.fr/Slashem/index.html#dungeonmap>, but only
against 0.0.7E7F2.

The original discussion of this patch can be found in this thread on RGRN
<http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_frm/thread/8e2751a7fc85fd6b>.

There are two new commands:

  * #overview (ctrl-o) - displays dungeon map overview
  * #annotate (ctrl-n, if using numpad) - names current level

While playing and descending deeper into the dungeon, the dungeon map
overview fills up with a description of fountains, altars, stores, temples,
sinks, thrones, trees and dungeon branches that are encountered.

This patch is already installed in the current version of UnNetHack on the
public server <telnet://un.nethack.nu/>.

Here's a screenshot of the dungeon map overview in-game:
<http://unnethack.files.wordpress.com/2010/03/dungeon-map-overview.png>

